[INGEST:vendor="docker", product="ai_gov", target_dataset="docker_ai_gov_raw", no_hit=keep]
// Docker AI Governance audit records.
//
// The HTTP Collector already parses `timestamp` into a native date before
// ingest -- it is not the RFC 3339 string the vendor reference describes, and
// not an epoch number either. Verified against live tenant data, so no
// string parsing or to_timestamp() conversion is needed or possible.
//
// Without this rule `_time` defaults to ingestion time, which ran ~30 seconds
// behind event time in the live stream. That skew would misorder events in a
// session timeline and shift them across correlation search windows.
//
// Records without a usable timestamp are kept (no_hit=keep) and fall back to
// ingestion time. Dropping a governance denial because its clock was malformed
// would lose exactly the record that matters most.
filter timestamp != null
| alter _time = timestamp;
